\description{
Inner-loop function for \code{fit()}. Takes a single config row from the
evaluate() leaderboard at evaluate()'s hyperparameters or, with
\code{final_bayesian_iter} above 0 (by default it is 0), re-tunes it with
warm-start Bayesian optimization from them and d points drawn around them
from a local grid (\code{build_warmstart_grid()}), for d tuned parameters,
keeping evaluate()'s unless the best candidate beats them by the margin
(\code{choose_member_params()}); then generates OOF predictions, fits a final
deployable model, evaluates on the held-out test set, and detects
performance degradation.

This function is the \strong{capture layer} — it runs silently and returns a
structured list. All console output (tree rendering, progress messages) is
the responsibility of the calling \code{fit()} function.

Each fold's recipe is prepped once, as in \code{\link[=evaluate_single_config]{evaluate_single_config()}},
and members of one preprocessing and selection read one prep's entry
(\code{prep_fold_entry()}): the warm-start re-tune, its Bayesian iterations
and the out-of-fold predictions run a workflow of the model alone on the
folds assembled from them (\code{assemble_folds()}), which keep
the positions of the rows they were cut from, so each out-of-fold
prediction's \code{.row} names its sample. The final fit runs the whole
workflow on \code{train_data}, so the stored workflow, and with it \code{predict()},
the prediction intervals and the applicability domain, bakes new rows
through the whole recipe.

The member is one unit (\code{run_unit()}): a run failure in any step ends it,
and the member records the step (\code{UNIT_STEPS}), the cause, its root class
and, with \code{keep_traces}, its backtrace. A door, internal or dependency
error is not the member's and propagates. UQ, measured coverage, AD and
slimming run as units of their own inside it: one that fails costs the
member only what it computes, and the member says so with a \code{skipped}
warning (slimming: a note).
}
